# CUDA / GPU (MBS)

Adapted from awesome-cursorrules Linux NVIDIA CUDA Python rule; retargeted to
this project's pins (not the upstream quantization app).

## Host constraints

- Driver is CUDA **12.8**-class; Linux/Windows torch wheels use the **cu128**
  index in `pyproject.toml`. Do not switch to PyPI's default cu130 wheel without
  a matching driver.
- Verify with `nvidia-smi` and `torch.cuda.is_available()` when changing torch
  pins.
- Hugging Face / torch caches belong under `$MBS_CACHE_ROOT`, never `$HOME`.

## Coding

- Write device-agnostic code (`cpu` / `cuda`); fail clearly if CUDA is required
  but missing.
- Prefer modest default batch sizes; profile before large GPU allocations.
- Do not recursively scan `*.pt` / `*.ckpt` / `*.pth` under artifact roots;
  use manifests and checksums.
- MethylGPT stays in `.venv-methylgpt` (torch pin conflict); see
  `docs/STATIC_FEATURES.md`.
- CpGPT full-model import (`torchtune` → `torchao.dtypes.nf4tensor`) currently
  fails on the MBS cu128 / torchao pin. Offline static export uses
  `mbs.static_features.cpgpt_adapter` instead of `CpGPTInferencer`; see
  `docs/STATIC_FEATURES.md`.
